cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ALPSbox in your research, please cite this software, the ALPS method paper, and the reference-implementation software and paper listed in references."
title: "ALPSbox: one-click DTI-ALPS processing with quality control and HTML reports"
type: software
url: "https://github.com/czf-chen/alpsbox"
authors:
  - name: "ALPSbox contributors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24137518"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Per-subject and batch DTI-ALPS processing on top of FSL/MRtrix3. Inputs are
  DICOM/NIfTI diffusion data with bval/bvec (and BIDS JSON for full eddy).
  The pipeline performs Gibbs unringing, eddy-current/motion correction
  (with outlier-slice replacement), brain extraction, tensor fitting and
  reorientation with vecreg, ROI extraction on the JHU-ICBM-FA-1mm template,
  and computes the ALPS index. Every subject receives eight categories of
  quality-control checks (including a registration-robustness metric), a
  recorded processing definition, and a single-file HTML report; CSV/JSON
  exports are provided for downstream statistics. GUI and CLI are bilingual
  (English/Chinese). FSL is not redistributed.
keywords:
  - DTI-ALPS
  - glymphatic system
  - diffusion MRI
  - neuroimaging
  - FSL
  - quality control
